<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Holy Roman Emperor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Holy Roman Emperor was the elected ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, a title that originated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a>'s coronation in 962 CE and was formally given up by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> in 1806. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> held it alongside the Spanish crown. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>, also Holy Roman Emperor, obtained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from the Ayyubid sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a> in 1229.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Holy Roman Emperor" width="276" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hans_Burgkmair_d._%C3%84._005.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
